Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_ojpeg.c
Line: 1992
Function: OJPEGReadHeaderInfoSecStreamSos
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: The code writes sp->sos_cs[sp->plane_sample_offset + o] (and sp->sos_tda[...] at line 1996) for o in [0, sp->samples_per_pixel_per_plane) without validating that plane_sample_offset + sp->samples_per_pixel_per_plane fits within the fixed-size arrays (size 4, consistent with 0..3 indexing used for JPEG tables). A malicious file that sets SamplesPerPixelPerPlane > 4 (or a nonzero plane_sample_offset combined with large count) will overflow these arrays.

Source context:
